// A project that COMPILES and declares NOT ONE `test`. A zero-test run exits 1 on purpose: a suite
// that has stopped containing tests reads exactly like a suite where everything passes, and that is
// the failure the command exists to prevent.
//
// ⚠ The file is a `*.test.maxon` holding no `test`, rather than an ordinary `.maxon`, and that
// sharpens the case rather than weakening it: it proves the runner counts `test` DECLARATIONS and
// not test FILES. (It is also the corpus's structural rule, enforced by `test-command/fixtures`.)
function greeting() returns String
	return "hello"
end 'greeting'
